{title: Big River}
{artist: Johnny Cash}
{key: E}
{# Источник: ручной перенос с UG. Intro-таб — в songs/raw/big-river.ug.txt. }

{comment: Intro}
(riff — таб в raw)

{comment: Verse 1}
Now I [E]taught the weeping willow how to cry,
And I showed the clouds how to cover up a clear blue [F#]sky. [B7]
And the [E]tears that I cried for that woman are gonna flood you Big [A]River.
Then I'm [E]gonna sit right [B7]here until I [E]die

{comment: Verse 2}
I [E]met her accidentally in St. Paul (Minnesota).
And it tore me up every time I heard her drawl, southern [F#]drawl. [B7]
Then I [E]heard my dream was back downstream cavortin' in Daven[A]port,
And I [E]followed you, Big [B7]River, when you [E]called.

{comment: Instrumental}
(ad lib)

{comment: Verse 3}
Then you [E]took me to St. Louis later on (down the river).
A freighter said she's been here but she's gone, boy, she's [F#]gone. [B7]
I [E]found her trail in Memphis, but she just walked up the [A]bluff.
She raised a few [E]eyebrows and then she [B7]went on down a[E]lone.

{comment: Verse 4}
Now, won't you [E]batter down by Baton Rouge, River Queen, roll it on.
Take that woman on down to New Orleans, New Or[F#]leans. [B7]
Go [E]on, I've had enough, dump my blues down in the [A]gulf.
[E]She loves you, Big [B7]River, more than [E]me.

{comment: Instrumental}
(ad lib)

{comment: Verse 5}
Now I [E]taught the weeping willow how to cry, cry, cry,
And I showed the clouds how to cover up a clear blue [F#]sky. [B7]
And the [E]tears that I cried for that woman are gonna flood you Big [A]River.
Then I'm [E]gonna sit right [B7]here until I [E]die. [E7]
